{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1702","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"A. Round Down the Price"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1 second"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"256 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"At the store, the salespeople want to make all prices "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"round"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":". "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In this problem, a number that is a power of $$$10$$$ is called a "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"round"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" number. For example, the numbers $$$10^0 = 1$$$, $$$10^1 = 10$$$, $$$10^2 = 100$$$ are "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"round"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" numbers, but $$$20$$$, $$$110$$$ and $$$256$$$ are not "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"round"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" numbers. "}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"So, if an item is worth $$$m$$$ bourles (the value of the item is not greater than $$$10^9$$$), the sellers want to change its value to the nearest "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"round"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" number that is not greater than $$$m$$$. They ask you: by how many bourles should you "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"decrease"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" the value of the item to make it worth exactly $$$10^k$$$ bourles, where the value of $$$k$$$ — is the maximum possible ($$$k$$$ — any non-negative integer)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For example, let the item have a value of $$$178$$$-bourles. Then the new price of the item will be $$$100$$$, and the answer will be $$$178-100=78$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of input data contains a single integer $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$) — the number of test cases ."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test case is a string containing a single integer $$$m$$$ ($$$1 \\le m \\le 10^9$$$) — the price of the item."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case, output on a separate line a single integer $$$d$$$ ($$$0 \\le d \\lt m$$$) such that if you reduce the cost of the item by $$$d$$$ bourles, the cost of the item will be the maximal possible "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"round"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" number. More formally: $$$m - d = 10^k$$$, where $$$k$$$ — the maximum possible non-negative integer."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n7\n1\n2\n178\n20\n999999999\n9000\n987654321\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n0\n1\n78\n10\n899999999\n8000\n887654321\n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the example:"}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"attrs":{"ordered":false},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$1 - 0 = 10^0$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$2 - 1 = 10^0$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$178 - 78 = 10^2$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$20 - 10 = 10^1$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$999999999 - 899999999 = 10^8$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$9000 - 8000 = 10^3$$$, "}],"kind":"list_item"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":" $$$987654321 - 887654321 = 10^8$$$. "}],"kind":"list_item"}],"kind":"list"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note that in each test case, we get the maximum possible "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"round"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" number."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"A","problemCode":"1702A","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1702/problem/A"}